ood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the disposition when the currency check itself cannot run (no network / no remote / detached HEAD): does it fail-open (warn but proceed) or fail-closed (block), and add a defect-seeded case for that path so a can't-check condition is not silently read as 'not stale'.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.failure-disposition-contract","E5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.23,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC2: 'it does not rely solely on a file that the stale tree also lacks. State how it establishes currency.'","AC4 covers only the fire case (a tree behind main whose plan is empty) — it does not cover the case where the check cannot compute currency (offline / no remote / detached HEAD).","ABSENCE: no disposition word (fail-open warn vs fail-closed block) stated for the currency-establishment step failing."],"finding":"The plan does not state what the check does when it cannot establish currency at all — e.g. no network to fetch the tracked branch, a detached HEAD, or a checkout with no configured remote. If the check fails-open (silent pass) in these cases it silently reintroduces the exact hazard (an operation that didn't happen, reported as success); if it fails-closed it may block legitimate offline runs. The disposition of the check's OWN failure is unstated.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f90a8f3513166b936","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC2 / AC4","norm_id":"n1fba0a650cf57612","priority":0.67,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an AC: 'When currency cannot be determined (offline, no tracked remote, detached HEAD), the tool emits an explicit UNDETERMINED/WARN signal distinct from both stale and current — never a silent pass.' Extend AC4 to seed this can't-check case.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"State how the currency baseline is kept authoritative — whether the check performs/requires a fresh fetch of the tracked branch, and how it behaves when the remote is unreachable (fail-loud vs. fail-open) — so a stale or unfetched local origin/main ref cannot itself produce a false 'not stale' reading.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.13,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC2: 'The check is not defeated by the stale tree itself ... State how it establishes currency.'","AC5 requires it to work 'for a developer running terraform locally with no CI provider' — implying possible offline / never-fetched state where origin/main tracking ref is stale","AGENTS.md:472 shows currency is normally re-established via an explicit `git fetch origin` — a plain comparison to the local origin/main ref without a fetch is not authoritative"],"finding":"AC2 guards against relying on a file the stale tree lacks, but does not address the freshness or reachability of the currency BASELINE itself: any git-based check compares the working tree to a local `origin/main` remote-tracking ref, which can be arbitrarily stale (never fetched) or unavailable offline (AC5). A check reading a stale local ref would report 'not stale' and silently reproduce the exact false-negative this ticket exists to eliminate.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4a916f51ba297c88","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC2 (and interaction with AC5)","norm_id":"nc3db4ddf8d7f683b","priority":0.67,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A developer whose clone last fetched days ago runs terraform locally; the check compares against a stale local origin/main and reports 'current' though real origin/main has moved","An offline developer where fetch fails — the check must define whether that is fail-open (false 'current') or fail-loud"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an AC (or extend AC2) requiring the check to establish baseline currency actively (e.g. `git fetch`/`git ls-remote` against the tracked branch at check time) and to report an unreachable-remote condition distinctly from both 'stale' and 'current', so the comparison ref cannot be silently stale.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Name and verify the concrete currency-establishing primitive (git ancestry/count against a freshly-fetched remote-tracking ref) and state its behaviour under detached HEAD, shallow clone, and no-network conditions.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3812,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC2: 'State how it establishes currency' is posed as a requirement but the plan gives no candidate mechanism.","The established primitive is a git ancestry/count query (e.g. `git merge-base --is-ancestor origin/main HEAD`, `git rev-list --count HEAD..origin/main`) against a fetched remote-tracking ref; the plan asserts the need for such a check but does not name or verify the mechanism, and AC5 (portable, no CI provider) constrains it to local git availability plus network fetch.","ABSENCE: no statement of how currency is determined when origin/main is not fetched, in a shallow clone, or in detached HEAD."],"finding":"AC2 requires the check to 'establish currency' without relying on a file the stale tree also lacks, but the plan leaves the currency mechanism unspecified and does not resolve which git primitive establishes ancestry/behind-ness — the load-bearing capability of the whole ticket.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa4be5e97c55dc366","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC2","norm_id":"naae3358d84432953","priority":0.4188,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer picks a mechanism that itself fails silently on a shallow/offline clone, reproducing the very 'operation that did not happen, reported as success' class the plan warns against."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","no verification commands or testing plan referenced","AC item 'AC1 - A Terraform plan or apply executed against a tree that is behind the track' cites operational evidence (iac) that lives outside the codebase; tag it [non-codebase] — prefix the checkbox text with [non-codebase] so the completion verifier accepts a recorded attestation instead of failing to find code proof."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P7"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["destructive terms: destroy; no backup/dry-run/rollback nearby"],"finding":"Destructive/irreversible operation(s) with no stated safeguard.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4e1650fc06461e62","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"n4b1254c143290a68","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"State the safeguard (backup, dry-run, reversible migration, rollback) or justify the irreversibility explicitly (T4).","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the operational rule that distinguishes 'stale/behind' (must warn) from 'legitimately diverged feature branch' (must not block) — e.g. warn iff local HEAD is a strict ancestor of origin/main and behind it, and define the message for the diverged case.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.701,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC1: 'a tree that is behind the tracked branch is DETECTED'","Non-goals: 'Not preventing local terraform runs from a feature branch — that is legitimate.'","A feature branch may be neither at nor a strict ancestor of main; 'behind' (strict-ancestor-of-origin/main) vs 'diverged' is left to the executor."],"finding":"The definition of 'behind the tracked branch' is ambiguous when reconciled with the non-goal that permits feature-branch runs: the plan does not state how the check distinguishes a stale checkout (must warn) from a legitimately diverged feature branch (must NOT be blocked/forbidden).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd110f519b1da2bd5","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC1 / AC2 / Non-goals","norm_id":"n3b4563207e4caf24","priority":0.099,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Developer on a feature branch that branched from an older main runs terraform locally and gets a spurious staleness warning, or conversely a genuinely-stale main checkout is mis-classified as a feature branch and silenced."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an AC or design note: currency = local HEAD vs the fetched origin/main tip; warn when HEAD is a strict ancestor behind origin/main; on a diverged feature branch, emit an informational 'diverged from main' note rather than a staleness error.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State how currency is established (or how the check degrades) for a terraform tree that is NOT a git checkout with a configured remote (server-outside-checkout / vendored subproject), so the signal is not silently unavailable for that supported shape.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.portability"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan premise throughout: 'behind origin/main', AC2 'establishes currency', AC3 'runs against current main' — all presuppose a git remote/tracked branch.","Matrix cell: 'Project location and access: server outside the checkout' and 'Target project: Terraform subprojects in a monorepo' exported/vendored without .git."],"finding":"The currency-establishment mechanism is framed entirely as 'behind origin/main' / 'the tracked branch', which assumes the terraform tree is a git checkout with a configured upstream remote. A terraform subproject checked out without a remote (archive export, vendored copy, or an explicitly-located/server-outside-checkout workspace) has no tracked branch to compare against, so the check has nothing to establish currency from.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f382ba22da04d7b4f","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC1/AC2 and the 'Observed' section ('behind origin/main')","norm_id":"naa4323f15c41d35e","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A Terraform subproject deployed to a server outside a git checkout (no .git/remote): the currency check has no tracked branch to diff against and either errors or silently no-ops, giving the operator no staleness signal — the very gap the ticket closes for the git-checkout case remains open here."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In AC2, name the currency source per shape (git upstream when present; otherwise an explicit 'currency-source-unavailable' warning) rather than assuming origin/main universally.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"na","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Add a prior-art paragraph citing the established solutions to this exact hazard (e.g. Atlantis' merge/checkout strategy for out-of-date branches; Terraform's native 'Saved plan is stale' serial/lineage guard) and justify the chosen approach against them.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["The plan frames the problem as unique to this repo ('the same class that has recurred repeatedly in this repo') and reasons from first principles ('it was asked the wrong question'), with no reference to any external tooling that solves the same problem.","Retrieved source: Atlantis 'Checkout Strategy' (runatlantis.io/docs/checkout-strategy) documents the identical hazard — 'if users push branches that are out of date with main, then their terraform plan could be deleting some resources that were configured in the main branch' — which is the plan's 'worse direction' (recreating/undoing deletions), and offers a merge-checkout strategy as mitigation.","Retrieved sources: HashiCorp discuss + Stack Overflow describe Terraform's native 'Saved plan is stale' guard keyed on state serial/lineage — a distinct but adjacent established mechanism the plan does not mention.","ABSENCE: the plan never states whether it evaluated adopting a merge-based plan (Atlantis-style) or a git-ancestry check, nor why it is (re)building bespoke detection."],"finding":"The plan proposes a novel staleness-detection mechanism for terraform runs without considering the established prior art that addresses this exact hazard (Atlantis' merge/checkout strategy for out-of-date branches; HashiCorp's native 'Saved plan is stale' serial/lineage check), nor justifying its approach against them.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc46a5d2fdc38c0d3","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Whole plan; 'Why this belongs with tonight's other findings' and 'Acceptance criteria' (AC1/AC2)","norm_id":"n26f47abbf4e1b6ab","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer builds a bespoke check that overlaps with or diverges from patterns Terraform automation tooling already standardises, missing edge cases those tools handle (e.g. detached HEAD, missing remote-tracking ref)."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"na","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","